 BSE| Energy difference of last empty index to LUMO [eV]                 804.717
 BSE| Number of GW-corrected occupied MOs                                     13
 BSE| Number of GW-corrected empty MOs                                       591
 BSE|
 BSE| No truncation of BSE matrices applied
 BSE|
 BSE| Total peak memory estimate from BSE [GB]                         4.398E+00
 BSE| Peak memory estimate per MPI rank from BSE [GB]                      0.092
 BSE|
 BSE| Diagonalizing aux. matrix with size of A. This will take around 0.E+00 s.
 BSE| Diagonalizing C. This will take around 0.E+00 s.
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| **************************************************************************
 BSE| *      Full ("ABBA") Bethe Salpeter equation (BSE) (i.e. without TDA)    *
 BSE| **************************************************************************
 BSE|
 BSE| The excitations are calculated by diagonalizing the BSE without the TDA:
 BSE|
 BSE|                |A B| |X^n|       |1  0| |X^n|
 BSE|                |B A| |Y^n| = Ω^n |0 -1| |Y^n|
 BSE|
 BSE| i.e. in index notation:
 BSE|
 BSE|   sum_jb ( A_ia,jb   X_jb^n + B_ia,jb   Y_jb^n ) = Ω^n X_ia^n
 BSE| - sum_jb ( B_ia,jb   X_jb^n + A_ia,jb   Y_jb^n ) = Ω^n Y_ia^n
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| i,j:       occupied molecular orbitals, i.e. state in          [   1,  13]
 BSE| a,b:       unoccupied molecular orbitals, i.e. state in        [  14, 604]
 BSE| n:         Excitation index
 BSE|
 BSE| A_ia,jb = (ε_a-ε_i) δ_ij δ_ab + α * v_ia,jb - W_ij,ab
 BSE| B_ia,jb = α * v_ia,jb - W_ib,aj
 BSE|
 BSE| prelim Ref.: Eqs. (24-27),(30),(35)
 BSE| in PRB 92,045209 (2015); http://dx.doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.92.045209 .
 BSE|
 BSE| The BSE is solved for Ω^n and X_ia^n as a hermitian problem, e.g. Eq.(42)
 BSE| in PRB 92,045209 (2015); http://dx.doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.92.045209 .
 BSE|
 BSE| ε_...:                 GW quasiparticle energy
 BSE| δ_...:                 Kronecker delta
 BSE| α:                     spin-dependent factor
 BSE| v_...:                 Electron-hole exchange interaction
 BSE| W_... = 1/ϵ v_...:     Direct interaction screened by 
 BSE|                        dielectric function ϵ(ω=0)
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| The spin-dependent factor is for the requested Singlet is α = 2.0
 BSE|
